  "content": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the arithmetic problem using the given values $a=137$, $b=29$, and $c=11$.\n\nThe expression to compute is:\n$$ (a \\cdot b + c^3) - (a - b) \\cdot c $$\n\n### Step 1: Compute $a \\cdot b$\n$$ 137 \\times 29 $$\nBreaking this down:\n$$ 137 \\times 29 = 137 \\times (30 - 1) = 4110 - 137 = 3973 $$\nSo, $a \\cdot b = 3973$.\n\n### Step 2: Compute $c^3$\n$$ 11^3 = 11 \\times 11 \\times 11 $$\n$$ 11 \\times 11 = 121 $$\n$$ 121 \\times 11 = 1331 $$\nSo, $c^3 = 1331$.\n\n### Step 3: Compute the first parenthesis $(a \\cdot b + c^3)$\n$$ 3973 + 1331 $$\nPerforming the addition:\n$$\n\\begin{array}{r}\n3973 \\\\\n+\\ 1331 \\\\\n\\hline\n5304\n\\end{array}\n$$\nSo, the first part equals $5304$.\n\n### Step 4: Compute $(a - b)$\n$$ 137 - 29 $$\nPerforming the subtraction:\n$$\n\\begin{array}{r}\n137 \\\\\n-\\ 29 \\\\\n\\hline\n108\n\\end{array}\n$$\nSo, $a - b = 108$.\n\n### Step 5: Compute the second part $(a - b) \\cdot c$\n$$ 108 \\times 11 $$\nUsing the property $x \\cdot 11 = x \\cdot (10 + 1)$:\n$$ 108 \\times 10 = 1080 $$\n$$ 108 \\times 1 = 108 $$\n$$ 1080 + 108 = 118",
